{% if part == "Doc" %}	DONE:
	- added the meta data from the real book.
	- put in the tunes structure.
	- put in the chords (real book).
	- put in the tune (real book).
	- put in the double time vamp and the solo section as printed in the real book.
	- added youtube performances (the real book refers to Coltrane - 'His Greatest Years - Vol. 3').
	TODO:
	- check the chords (real book).
	- check the tune (real book).
	- hear the tune to check that it is right and adjust the tempo.
	- the rubato intro (bars 1-11) is handwritten with many ledger lines and is hard to read: check every note against a recording.
	- intro bar 2: the first A flat looks like a quarter note in the book, which leaves the bar a beat short; it is typed as a half note.
	- intro bar 3: the three beamed eighths have no triplet sign in the book; they are typed as a triplet so that the bar adds up.
	- intro bar 8: the book writes plain A and E (not A flat and E flat) in this bar; typed as printed.
	- A tempo bar 4: the book shows a half note E flat and a triplet starting with a rest, a beat short; the half note is typed dotted as in bar 12.
	- A tempo bars 6 and 14: the first half note is written just above the staff with no ledger line; typed as G flat (bar 6) and G (bar 14).
	REMARKS:
	- the real book marks the intro 'Rubato:' and the head 'A Tempo'. The last note of the intro has a rising line (a rip/fall-off sign) after it which is not typed.
	- the vamp after the head is marked 'Double X:' in the book with a circled 8 over a C-7 bar; it is typed as eight bars of C-7.
{% endif %}
